ould be used uh however the  the citation biospa system would be  uh preferable uh because of the the full  automation capabilities that could be uh  incorporated including the liquid  handling  uh question here is it better to use  labels for measuring  um for measuring size of a steroid  versus bright fields so it's better to  use labels for measuring proliferation  or um so this really is going to depend  on your biology  the primary readout is is going to be  the size of a steroid for  3d studies and this is determined by  gen 5 masking with diameter being  determined from  the mask applied to the to the spheroid  with then the option of extrapolating uh  theoretical volume from that assuming  assuming uh  symmetry um you know so so both of these  methods label label-free or fluorescence  are ultimately going to be used to  create that mask to define that  that area so you should expect to see  very comparable results across those two  methods  that being said i would say in many ways  labels  because of the potential impact on the  cells themselves and  potentially changing over time as  staining  flattens out or as the steam may break  down would make  label free more preferable um  one other thing i would add there is  that um as we are defining that spheroid  volume we're putting a mask we're using  our image analysis to define the border  of that volume  important consideration is how does that  volume change um  in maybe treatment-induced ways so this  is not necessarily  caused by changes in the cell number  but by the ability of those cells to  remain tightly packed into a spheroid  structure  so in other words you could likely see a  spheroid starting to break  up as it is being treated  and potentially that could be perceived  as an increase in volume  so one way this can be addressed is by  looking at the average signal or taking  the ratio of uh  signal intensity over the uh the area so  this is one way you can start to  identify  where maybe the the spheroid is breaking  up  instead of instead of actually changing  its size  um someone's asking can they run a  proliferation experiment  on the citation 5 without co2  um yeah the short answer is yes you can  although  you will want to i think make it a bit  more of a manual  process co2 is certainly going to be  essential to maintain  cell viability so in that case in the  absence of  a co2 hookup to the citation 5  you could run what we call a  discontinuous kinetic experiment so in  this case  the plate is red and then returned to  the incubator until the next reset and  then it would just be delivered  in that process moving forward to  continue to get read steps over the  desired  timeline  um how do you do how how can we derive  cell counts from steroid diameter  um the short answer is you really can't  um as i was describing  uh a bit a moment ago with the bright  fields versus label question  um different cells are going to pack  into into spheroids uh  shapes differently um so really what we  are what we are looking at there is is  just um within a given  condition how those those sizes will  change and we are really using  a volume of our cellulite as a proxy for  cell number  for studies that really do want to get  down to that granular detail  of the number of cells that are present  i would recommend um some of the  techniques i described with  this is so disassociating the the  steroids this is really kind of a  it's a powerful technique to get the  best of both worlds where you can get a  kinetic evaluation  of a steroid and the benefits of that  system  but then be able to break it up and  analyze it in much greater detail  for either using image-based methods or  flow cytometry this is also a powerful  technique  to get at if you really want to resolve  cells that are  internal to that spheroid that might not  be detectable with conventional imaging  methods  let's get a couple more here  could we simultaneously check for cell  viability and the proliferation as well  yeah so absolutely so the um the methods  i described there with proliferation  and the um the markers for apoptosis and  necrosis those can absolutely be done in  a single  assay so those read steps essentially  combined and we have  protocols that we can provide  for you that get you started in terms of  the basic setup and steps for doing that  but essentially it consists of the  proliferation read step coupled with  the fluorescent read steps to be able to  identify  the fluorescence in addition to  the actual cell number the total cell  number so that's really the power of  that system is that they are combined  and so that you have the ability to not  only say the number of cells present and  the number that are apoptotic on the  product  but the ratio of those that now allows  for much better comparison of those  samples  all right let's do one more here um  could you review good cell seating  techniques to achieve either  distribution of cells  um so yeah as i mentioned this really is  a critical  readout or sorry aspect of the setup  and the primary way i advise people to  improve this or improve the seating  density is to  want to make sure you have an even  distribution of cells a nice  homogeneous mix of cells or even the  distribution of cells within your  suspension  add an appropriate volume to your to  your wells i recommend about 200  microliters  per 96 well plate um  and letting this is a critical step you  let them just sit  it's hard to to kind of get out of um  maybe maybe conventions but rather than  popping that right into the incubator  let that plate sit at room temperature  in the hood that will allow the cells to  settle down  evenly remaining in that even  distribution and they'll give you a much  more  even layer of cells in your microplate  so after about 30 minutes then you can  you can move that back into the  incubator  um certainly recommend confirming that  so you can actually use  the amenities image analysis tools that  i described and we have some  specific kind of qc protocols that allow  you to go through an entire microplate  and assess  or confirm that you do have even  distribution of cells  before proceeding with the acid so this  is a valuable way to  to optimize an assay before proceeding  as you can imagine the starting number  of cells is really an important variable  in these assays  and can heavily skew the results and the  perceived proliferation rate so getting  that step right really does a lot in  terms of  optimizing results and giving you the  most meaningful  data all right well thank you again for  your time and great questions if there  are any other questions that come in  or ones i didn't get to i will follow up  uh by email  and make sure everybody does get an  answer to the questions and um  please follow up by email afterwards if  you uh if you think of something else  all right thank you joe thanks so much  unfortunately that's all the time we  have for today  and i just want to thank everyone who  joined us um as joe  said if we did not get to your question  that you submitted we'll be sure to  follow up with you in an email  and if you'd like more information about  biotech's products and services  please visit our website at  www.biotech.com  we hope you enjoyed today's presentation  and have a great rest of your day
 

